  "body": "Found by mkinney's QA run p05 (wrapped cylinder) and reproduced by a verification run on 2026-11-18, CamCraft main `83867fd7`.\n\nWhat happens: on a D50 bar with six blind D5 x 8 mm radial holes, two of them opposite each other, `detect_holes` returns `{\"holes\":1,\"radial_holes\":0}` with one hole `entry_z 25, floor_z -25, through: true` - a 50 mm through hole across the solid core.\n\nNot unsafe: generating it is refused (the drill is too short; with a long drill the gouge gate refuses the post, 44-50 mm into the model). The refusal text even suggests \"drill it with a longer drill, or in stages from both sides\".\n\nWorkaround: type the hole list by hand.\n\nDone means: blind radial holes are detected as separate holes with their own depth (or as radial holes for an indexed drill), pinned by a test with this bar.\n",
